      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 is specified in the netlist and SPICE deck as 0.1 uF / 16 V, connected between GND and Display_Power_Switch.",
      "expected": "The design specification states that C1 should be part of the 1 uF / 25 V capacitor set used in the PDI EPD driving circuit: C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"14\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"1\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"9\") (name \"Display_Power_Switch\") ... (node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C1 0 Display_Power_Switch 0.1u"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD power rail has one tenth of the intended capacitance, reducing decoupling and potentially causing display-driver voltage droop, noise, or instability during boost/charge-pump transients.",
      "confidence": 0.68
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the specified EPD driver implementation by using a 0.1 uF/16 V capacitor for C1 where the specification calls for 1 uF/25 V; this reduces the intended decoupling on the display power rail."
}

